KG42.register("rules-01d6f20ef4786730656d9a52",{"id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R005","paper":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R005","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Energy-trade execution","process_stage":"activation","market_meaning":"The energy sharing coordinator supervises the region's P2P energy-trading activities. Scope: General P2P energy-sharing framework recorded under M01; trading within an energy sharing region. The coordinator negotiates electricity purchases and sales with the retailer on behalf of the participants to balance energy within the region. Scope: The aggregate retailer-trading paradigm shown in Fig. 2 for an energy sharing region. Local P2P energy exchanges take place at the internal market price. Scope: General P2P paradigm recorded under M01; exchanges within the local market. Participants must first share energy with each other and then interact with the retailer through aggregated power. Scope: P2P energy sharing in grid-connected microgrids with one point of common coupling. Condition: The grid-connected microgrid has only one point of common coupling. P2P energy sharing is not used; all participants are instead considered to trade individually with the retailer. Scope: Simulation exit mechanism attributed to Ref. [17]. Condition: The maximum number of iterations is reached without convergence. P2P energy sharing remains in use based on the results of the last iteration. Scope: Simulation exit mechanism adopted in this paper; choice of trading arrangement upon termination. Condition: The simulation is forced to exit at the maximum number of iterations without convergence.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function execution.energy_trade under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["coordination.local_operator","execution.energy_trade","pricing.local"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R005-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"execution.energy_trade","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-e15"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R005-E002","source":"pricing.local","target":"execution.energy_trade","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R005-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"General P2P energy-sharing framework recorded under M01; trading within an energy sharing region. | General P2P paradigm recorded under M01; exchanges within the local market. | P2P energy sharing in grid-connected microgrids with one point of common coupling. | Simulation exit mechanism adopted in this paper; choice of trading arrangement upon termination. | Simulation exit mechanism attributed to Ref. [17]. | The aggregate retailer-trading paradigm shown in Fig. 2 for an energy sharing region.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e19"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The energy sharing coordinator supervises the region's P2P energy-trading activities. Scope: General P2P energy-sharing framework recorded under M01; trading within an energy sharing region.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The coordinator negotiates electricity purchases and sales with the retailer on behalf of the participants to balance energy within the region. Scope: The aggregate retailer-trading paradigm shown in Fig. 2 for an energy sharing region.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Local P2P energy exchanges take place at the internal market price. Scope: General P2P paradigm recorded under M01; exchanges within the local market.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Participants must first share energy with each other and then interact with the retailer through aggregated power. Scope: P2P energy sharing in grid-connected microgrids with one point of common coupling. Condition: The grid-connected microgrid has only one point of common coupling.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C005","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"P2P energy sharing is not used; all participants are instead considered to trade individually with the retailer. Scope: Simulation exit mechanism attributed to Ref. [17]. Condition: The maximum number of iterations is reached without convergence.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e19"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C006","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"P2P energy sharing remains in use based on the results of the last iteration. Scope: Simulation exit mechanism adopted in this paper; choice of trading arrangement upon termination. Condition: The simulation is forced to exit at the maximum number of iterations without convergence.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e19"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e03","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":4,"printed_page":"996","section":"3.1","anchor_text":"practice in many countries to set the export price in the FIT scheme co lower than the retail price.","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 1","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In the P2P energy sharing paradigm, the prosumers and consumers first share their generation and consumption in a local market at an internal price, and then trade with a retailer to cover the remaining electricity deficit or surplus. The internal price is usually set between the export price and the retail price, so that each prosumer or consumer, no matter it is an electricity seller or buyer, benefits from the P2P energy sharing."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":"996","section":"3.1","anchor_text":"gy sharing paradigm d P2P energy sharing paradigms. P2P energy sharing can be carried out among pros","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"P2P energy sharing can be carried out among prosumers in a microgrid or a part of distribution network (referred to as \"energy sharing region (ESR)\" in this paper), supervised by a market operator (named \"energy sharing coordinator\", short as \"coordinator\", in this paper). A coordinator is usually needed in P2P energy sharing practice due to two reasons. First of all, a coordinator is needed to specify the rules for trading and supervise the energy sharing activities. The rules include the core pricing model and implementation process, as well as other relevant rules to guarantee the interests of every participant. Secondly, a trading platform as well as the associated metering and billing mechanisms needs to be provided and operated by a coordinator, based on which P2P energy sharing is able to be conducted."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e15","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p07-c1r2__v141-a-M04-participation","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.3","anchor_text":"p y/ y gy balance within the energy sharing region. P2P energy sharing in grid- m connected microgri","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In the paradigm shown in Fig. 2, the coordinator negotiates with the retailer on behalf of all the prosumers to buy/sell electricity for energy balance within the energy sharing region. P2P energy sharing in grid-connected microgrids with only one point of common coupling (PCC) follows this paradigm, because the physical network structure requires that the prosumers have to share their energy with each other ﬁrst and then interact with the retailer in form of aggregated power [14–17]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e19","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p07-c2r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.3","anchor_text":"gy y g p g d- market mechanisms they designed [13,15,17,37]. C) If convergence cannot always be guar","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"exception"},"source_text":"If convergence cannot always be guaranteed, an exit mechanism is usually designed in P2P energy sharing mechanisms, as that in Ref. [17], because in real life participants need to settle their trades ﬁnally and cannot just wait forever, although the speciﬁcs of the exit mechanism can vary. For example, in Ref. [17], if the simulation does not converge when the maximum number of iterations is reached, then the simulation is forced to exit, and all the prosumers are considered to directly trade with the retailer individually instead (i.e. P2P energy sharing is not used given divergence). For the exit mechanism used in this paper (which will be detailed later in Section 3.3.4), the simulation is also forced to exit at the maximum number of iterations if not converge, but the status at the last iteration is used for settling trades (i.e. P2P energy sharing is still used based on the results of the last iteration)."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"The frozen C1 graph declares no typed x objects for this rule; its field note states that typed variable objects are outside the graph draft and this does not assert that the source lacks variables. The supplied evidence for R005 describes coordinator roles, qualitative trading arrangements and fallback choices rather than source-defined design or operational decision variables, so no x object is formalized here.","empty_theta_reason":"The frozen C1 graph declares no typed theta objects for this rule; its field note states that typed parameter objects are outside the graph draft and this does not assert that the source lacks parameters. The supplied evidence for R005 provides no fixed parameter value, coefficient or domain for this rule, so no theta object is formalized here."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M04-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"execution.energy_trade","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e05","quote":"First of all, a coordinator is needed to specify the rules for trading and supervise the energy sharing activities."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e15","quote":"In the paradigm shown in Fig. 2, the coordinator negotiates with the retailer on behalf of all the prosumers to buy/sell electricity for energy balance within the energy sharing region."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e03","quote":"the prosumers and consumers first share their generation and consumption in a local market at an internal price"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e15","quote":"P2P energy sharing in grid-connected microgrids with only one point of common coupling (PCC) follows this paradigm, because the physical network structure requires that the prosumers have to share their energy with each other ﬁrst and then interact with the retailer in form of aggregated power [14–17]."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e19","quote":"For example, in Ref. [17], if the simulation does not converge when the maximum number of iterations is reached, then the simulation is forced to exit, and all the prosumers are considered to directly trade with the retailer individually instead (i.e. P2P energy sharing is not used given divergence)."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e19","quote":"For the exit mechanism used in this paper (which will be detailed later in Section 3.3.4), the simulation is also forced to exit at the maximum number of iterations if not converge, but the status at the last iteration is used for settling trades (i.e. P2P energy sharing is still used based on the results of the last iteration)."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"9040b50317fc41e2b9b3e8cafee86c384158d56122f4ec9b0403cd7d3a8493e0","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The frozen R005 constraints express coordination/supervision, retailer negotiation, qualitative local-exchange pricing, local-first/retailer-aggregated interaction, and two non-convergence fallback arrangements. The supplied B evidence for this rule is qualitative process wording and contains no supported equation, objective, domain, or numeric parameter specification for R005 itself. The rule is therefore treated as non-mathematical for this formulation, without asserting that the wider source lacks mathematical variables or parameters.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","execution.energy_trade"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R005-E001"],"rationale":"C001 states the coordinator's supervision of local P2P trading, matching the coordination.local_operator -> execution.energy_trade relation carried by E001."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","execution.energy_trade"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R005-E001"],"rationale":"C002 states the coordinator negotiates with the retailer on behalf of participants for regional energy balance, an execution.energy_trade relation originating from coordination.local_operator and represented on E001."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C003","node_ids":["pricing.local","execution.energy_trade"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R005-E002"],"rationale":"C003 states local P2P exchanges occur at the internal market price, linking pricing.local to execution.energy_trade through E002."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C004","node_ids":["execution.energy_trade"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C004 constrains the sequencing of execution.energy_trade: local sharing first, then aggregated retailer interaction. No additional frozen edge expresses this sequencing."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C005","node_ids":["execution.energy_trade"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C005 specifies a non-convergence fallback in which P2P sharing is not used and participants trade individually with the retailer; it is a branch on execution.energy_trade."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C006","node_ids":["execution.energy_trade"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C006 specifies the alternative non-convergence fallback in which P2P sharing remains in use on last-iteration results; it is a branch on execution.energy_trade."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
